title: Chastened as Sons – Doctrine of Assurance
description: God chastens every son He receives: the Father's correction of His saved children in this life, even unto death, and never the loss of salvation. From the teachings on Hebrews 12, David, Ananias and Sapphira, and 1 Corinthians 5.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-assurance-chastened-as-sons.html

# Built from the "Chastened as sons" teachings in studies/data/topics/assurance.json, in the author's words.

=== Introduction
# from 7039
--- Chastened as Sons [title]
overline: Doctrine · Assurance
heading: Chastened as Sons
sub: He chastises those he loves and scourges every son.
refs: Hebrews 12:6-8; 2 Samuel 12:13; 1 Corinthians 5:5
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the study. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 2535, 4826
--- Whom the Lord loveth he chasteneth
big: Hebrews 12:6
lead: God chastises His own for our iniquity. He takes the rod to His children when they sin.
callout: We are punished here on earth for our sins. Sometimes very harshly. Sometimes with death.

=== Punished, yet not lost
# from 4826, 14249
--- The Lord hath put away thy sin
big: 2 Samuel 12:13
lead: And so God punished David, yet He put away David's sin, because he had the imputed righteousness of Jesus Christ. His faith in God's word.
p: We who are saved in Christ shall not die. But in this life we will be punished, that we may learn and the glory of God be known, not just by His mercy but His wrath. As an example for others.

# from 2535
--- Ananias and Sapphira
kicker: Acts 5
lead: Were Ananias and Sapphira saved? The Bible says in Acts 4 that the entire church was of one heart and one soul. They were of that church. I think the implication is clear they were.
p: But their being in Heaven when they die, justified by faith and Jesus' imputed righteousness didn't keep them from sinning, nor did it stop God from punishing them with their lives.
refs: Acts 4:32; Acts 5:3-5; Acts 5:9-10

# from 2535
--- Chastened unto death
panel-warn: The fruit inspectors | Many of the religion of works, who maintain that you must repent of sinning to be saved, and claim that the Gospel of Christ, salvation by faith in grace, is a “license to sin.” And so, being fruit inspectors, take this story as evidence they were not believers.
panel: What it shows | But what it shows is that God chastises His own for our iniquity. He takes the rod to His children when they sin. The Bible says He scourges His adopted sons and daughters. Even unto death.
callout: We saved are held to a higher standard than the unsaved, and we are punished here in this earth, sometimes more so than the unsaved, who are not God's children.

# from 14971
--- Delivered unto Satan
scripture: 1 Corinthians 5:4-5 | mark: that the spirit may be saved in the day of the Lord Jesus
p: Paul tells them to church discipline him, that he be given over to Satan for destruction of the flesh, even if his spirit is saved. God allows Satan to destroy us in the flesh.
p: The hope in church discipline is that the person gets right. Sees their error and comes back. But if not, at least in death they are free from the sin and present with the Lord.
callout: Note this teaches OSAS.

# from 11437, 16199, 7776
--- Called home, still saved
lead: If they remain backslidden, God may call them home. **But they are still saved.**
panel-warn: Thyatira | Backslidden and defiant, Jesus says He will punish her and those who are with her. He chasteneth who He loves. These aren't some sort of reprobates like the Nicolaitanes, these are His servants gone astray.
panel: Just, but not eternal | We know that judgment is just, but not eternal, because once saved always saved. God will take a backslidden Christian home in chastisement.
refs: Revelation 2:20-23; Ezekiel 18:31-32

=== Much is required
# from 13935, 14453
--- To whom much is given
big: Luke 12:48 | mark: unto whomsoever much is given, of him shall be much required
p: It should also be a warning to us that know better. That our knowledge and understanding means that should we stray from the goodness of God, we should expect a much worse punishment for it.
p: We do not have a license to sin and disobedience is met with punishment and chastisements from our Father. Many a great Christian has fallen to this, backslidden and ruined in this life. Lacking proper fear of the Lord.
refs: 1 Samuel 6:19

# from 16329
--- The way of the Lord is not equal
kicker: Ezekiel 33
panel-warn: The misreading | Many make the entire message spiritual, and apply this to salvation, that you can lose salvation or that we must turn from our sins to be saved.
panel: The chastening of believers | Again, this applies to chastening of believers. We are saved by grace through faith, not of ourselves. It is a gift of God.
p: But the blessings of this world come when you are right with God. And He withdraws His protection when those who call themselves by His name don't walk in His ways.
callout: If you've stopped, you aren't right with God. If you aren't right, get right. Life is but a vapour. The time is now.
refs: Ezekiel 33:17-20; Hebrews 10:31

# from 16028
--- The proud believer
big: Daniel 4:37
lead: Too many Christians get comfortable in the blessings and protection God provides us. Like Nebuchadnezzar, we not only take things for granted, but begin to pridefully take credit for the things in our life that are by the grace of God.
p: Don't be surprised if you continue down the road, backslidden, to have this type of punishment. I have both observed it and experienced a fraction of it. Don't let it happen to you!

=== Sons in the Father's house
# from 7039
--- Abraham's repeated lie
kicker: Genesis 12 · Genesis 20
lead: If he, a mighty man of faith, called “a friend of God,” struggled with sin and fear, then we can know the same is true of us.
p: But we can also see that God saves us regardless of our fear or lack of faith. He chastises those he loves and scourges every son. He often will expose us to embarrassment and humiliation in exposing our sin. But it is to our benefit, as it is here for Abraham.
refs: Genesis 20:13; James 2:23

# from 14236
--- Secret sin and the Father's rod
scripture: Psalm 90:8; Luke 8:17
p: That fearful looking for judgment, the guilt we feel when we disobey God's word, the pangs of our conscience, is a powerful motivation to get right with the Lord.
callout: Especially knowing that, as adopted children, our Father will not spare the rod, and the sins we do in secret will be revealed in the light.

# from 15133, 15330
--- The prodigal chastened
kicker: Rehoboam · 2 Chronicles 12
p: Very familiar to a lot of Christians, who after conversion and with the support of those before them to edify them, do great things for the Lord and are blessed, but soon their passion dies and they turn from the path of righteousness. And God chastens them. But He is merciful to send His word as warning before destruction to get right with Him.
big: Hosea 12:6
callout: The same promise to the saved, who may backslide and be chastened. Turn back to the Lord and be forgiven.
refs: 2 Chronicles 12:5-7

# from 15133, 8808
--- Always welcome
lead: If you're in rebellion now, repent. You are always welcome in the Father's house, as sons and daughters. He will deliver you from what you deserve, that you may have a chance to serve Him.
p: Always let your sons and daughters know they are loved no matter what, even in chastisement. That they always have a way back and know it, terms that are fair, and that it's offered in love. Don't spare the rod, but don't forget mercy and grace.

# from 14601, 13156
--- Grace toward the brother
panel-warn: “Works come automatically” | There are quite a few professing Christians and even entire denominations that teach that works come automatically, and without evidence of a changed life, we should doubt the salvation of someone.
panel: Encourage rather than condemn | We should be careful to be understanding rather than judgmental. To encourage rather than condemn. Not to condone sin. But to not be confrontationally judgmental.
callout: If they have repented, and asked to be forgiven, we are to treat them as if they'd never sinned. For we were once bondmen in Egypt.

=== Summary
# from 2535, 4826, 14971, 11437, 13935, 16329, 15133
--- In summary
point: Every son | God chastises His own for our iniquity. He takes the rod to His children when they sin.
point: Punished, not lost | God punished David, yet He put away David's sin. We who are saved in Christ shall not die.
point: Even unto death | God will take a backslidden Christian home in chastisement. But they are still saved.
point: Much is required | Our knowledge and understanding means that should we stray, we should expect a much worse punishment for it.
point: Not a license to sin | The blessings of this world come when you are right with God.
point: Always welcome | Turn back to the Lord and be forgiven.

